            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the inpatient treatment of your patient, a 57-year-old female, admitted on 18/10/2024 due to acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Blood tests showed mild systemic inflammation. She was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebuliser, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, resulting in significant clinical improvement. Spirometry was performed prior to discharge, confirming moderate obstructive ventilatory impairment. Patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation self-management was provided. She was discharged in stable condition and is referred back to your care for ongoing COPD management. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you have any questions.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
